  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ukraine compliance with EU industrial policies</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As a result of the project, a comprehensive analysis will identify the specific European Union (EU) legislation that needs to be implemented by Ukraine to align with the EU acts in direct relation to Enterprise and Industrial policy compliance with the EU acquis- Chapter 20 of EU accession requirements. This analysis will also highlight the existing gaps in Ukrainian legislation that must be addressed to expedite the country&apos;s integration into the EU. The EU acquis- Chapter 20 of EU accession requirements covers Industrial Policy, Skills, Corporate Social Responsibility, Cooperative Societies, Late payment Directive for the strategic economic sectors of Ukraine.The project has a positive impact on:&#x2022;	SDG 8; Inclusive and sustainable economic growth: support productive activities, decent job creation, entrepreneurship, creativity and innovation.&#x2022;	SDG9; Promote inclusive and sustainable industrialization and foster innovation; increase access to finance for small- and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs), upgrade the technological capabilities of industrial sectors.</narrative>
  </description>
